namespace trion:
    use software

    section "Files, packages and namespaces":
        A source file means a file that holds statements of the trion language.
        A package means a directory that holds a manifest and source files.
        A manifest means the file "trion.toml" of a package.
        An entry file means the source file that a manifest names.
        A namespace means a named group of terms and statements.
        A section means a titled group of statements inside a namespace.
        A dependency means a package that a manifest names.
        The standard library means the packages that the trion project provides for reuse.

        Each package has exactly one manifest.
        Each manifest names exactly one entry file.
        Each source file belongs to exactly one package.
        Each statement belongs to exactly one namespace.

        [DOCUMENT-INCLUDE]
        The trion processor shall read each source file that the entry file includes.

        [DOCUMENT-USE]
        Where a namespace uses a namespace of a dependency, the trion processor shall resolve the terms of that dependency.

        [DOCUMENT-SECTION-NO-MEANING]
        A section shall add no contract to a specification.
